WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.679
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.949 --> 00:13.129
I can't believe such a big exercise... was ordered without any notice.

3
00:13.129 --> 00:16.829
The schedule is one thing, but I'm worried about the nature of the assignment.

4
00:16.829 --> 00:20.889
We're not a recon unit. Having regular infantry play the opposing force is a bit...

5
00:20.889 --> 00:24.089
I don't know the details, but one thing is clear.

6
00:24.089 --> 00:28.674
This is an order, and according to it, 2nd Company is going.

7
00:30.609 --> 00:33.529
And another thing that's certain is,

8
00:33.529 --> 00:36.859
I feel sorry that you have a battalion commander like me.

9
00:38.247 --> 00:39.539
Sir, why would you say that?

10
00:39.539 --> 00:41.922
I'm especially sorry to our 2nd Company Commander.

11
00:41.922 --> 00:43.089
It's a critical time for you...

12
00:43.089 --> 00:47.909
No, sir. It's a critical time for me, but it's the same for you, sir.

13
00:47.909 --> 00:54.493
It must be harder for you to carry out such a heavy, or frankly, excessive order.

14
00:56.049 --> 00:59.449
It's because you two are doing so well.

15
01:00.449 --> 01:02.019
Is that so?

16
01:02.769 --> 01:06.209
Then let's do a good job this time too!

17
01:06.209 --> 01:09.428
Exactly! Why not trust our soldiers?

18
01:09.428 --> 01:11.764
Yes, let's do that!

19
01:15.242 --> 01:18.569
That was the atmosphere in the battalion commander's office.

20
01:18.569 --> 01:20.909
I was so surprised.

21
01:20.909 --> 01:23.469
I'm sorry for calling you out so late.

22
01:23.469 --> 01:25.209
- Not at all. - It's fine, sir.

23
01:25.209 --> 01:27.879
It looked like you were having a drink.

24
01:27.879 --> 01:29.294
No, sir!

25
01:29.294 --> 01:33.475
- I was just... - You're off duty, so it's fine.

26
01:34.974 --> 01:36.329
Company Commander...

27
01:36.329 --> 01:40.589
Isn't there usually a specific unit in charge of the opposing force?

28
01:40.589 --> 01:44.146
That's right. Or at least a recon unit, as far as I know.

29
01:44.146 --> 01:46.609
Right? So why are we doing it?

30
01:46.609 --> 01:50.609
It's an order that came down from the top.

31
01:50.609 --> 01:53.775
Of course, our 2nd Company personnel are excellent,

32
01:53.775 --> 01:57.649
but I'm a bit worried about whether we can fulfill that role well.

33
01:57.649 --> 01:59.329
Exactly.

34
02:00.989 --> 02:04.429
But Company Commander, you're currently up for promotion review.

35
02:04.429 --> 02:07.742
Will this training affect that?

36
02:07.742 --> 02:11.369
Whether we succeed or not, would I even get promoted?

37
02:11.369 --> 02:16.009
Still, couldn't the result change depending on the success of this training?

38
02:16.009 --> 02:18.549
The announcement is soon. Would it even be reflected?

39
02:18.549 --> 02:21.229
Seeing the battalion commander apologize,

40
02:21.229 --> 02:24.349
he must be under more pressure than I am.

41
02:24.349 --> 02:29.629
The regimental commander recommended him after seeing his report, so...

42
02:29.629 --> 02:32.089
- Ddong Il Gu. - Yes, sir.

43
02:32.089 --> 02:33.549
This isn't easy for you either, right?

44
02:33.549 --> 02:36.409
- I... - If you were still an enlisted soldier,

45
02:36.409 --> 02:39.326
you'd be like, "Fuck, why do we have to do this?

46
02:39.326 --> 02:40.849
They're totally dumping this on us."

47
02:40.849 --> 02:45.009
- Right? - When did I ever say that...

48
02:45.009 --> 02:47.809
Well, it's a mission we have to do anyway!

49
02:47.809 --> 02:50.309
Let's do our best until we leave for training!

50
02:50.309 --> 02:52.069
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

51
02:52.069 --> 02:55.384
Who knows? Our boys might do an amazing job again.

52
02:55.384 --> 02:59.064
At a glance, they almost look like special forces.

53
02:59.989 --> 03:00.989
I agree.

54
03:00.989 --> 03:04.789
I'll tell the boys tomorrow, so be prepared for their resentment.

55
03:04.789 --> 03:05.809
- Yes, sir! - Understood.

56
03:05.809 --> 03:07.309
- Shall we dismiss? - Yes!

57
03:07.309 --> 03:09.253
Good work!

58
03:09.896 --> 03:11.829
- Hey, hey. - I'll head in first!

59
03:11.829 --> 03:14.838
- Chungseong! Love you, sir! - Take good care of Il Gu.

60
03:17.229 --> 03:21.629
- What about you, sir? - Oh, I'll head in after tidying up.

61
03:21.629 --> 03:26.689
Don't worry too much, okay? What's going to happen will happen...

62
03:26.689 --> 03:28.259
I'm not worried.

63
03:28.259 --> 03:30.669
Good. Everything will be fine.

64
03:30.669 --> 03:33.469
Of course! Thank you, First Sergeant! Let's do this!

65
03:33.469 --> 03:34.629
- Fighting! - Yes, sir!

66
03:34.629 --> 03:36.638
- I'll get going then! - Yes, sir. Take care.

67
03:36.638 --> 03:39.078
- Get inside quickly. - Yes, sir.

68
03:58.969 --> 04:01.729
Lights on! Everyone, wake up!

69
04:01.729 --> 04:04.389
[EP08. The Unsent Will]

70
04:04.389 --> 04:05.912
Jeon Sekai!

71
04:05.912 --> 04:07.372
Private First Class Jeon Sekai!

72
04:07.372 --> 04:08.999
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam,

73
04:08.999 --> 04:10.959
5 days till discharge!

74
04:10.959 --> 04:13.929
Whoa, congratulations!

75
04:13.929 --> 04:17.129
I should've saved my final leave and used it now instead.

76
04:17.129 --> 04:19.609
At least you went. Mine got canceled.

77
04:19.609 --> 04:24.949
Still, it's nice to be together thanks to that.

78
04:24.949 --> 04:26.909
- That's true. - You're right.

79
04:26.909 --> 04:32.448
To mark D-5 till discharge, there's a surprise event in a bit.

80
04:32.448 --> 04:34.057
Yes, sir.

81
04:34.057 --> 04:36.380
- Hyeon Uk! - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

82
04:36.380 --> 04:39.989
- Morning coffee? - I'd love that.

83
04:39.989 --> 04:41.656
- Sergeant Kim Sang Hun! - Yeah?

84
04:41.656 --> 04:44.494
May I take a quick coffee break with Hyeon Uk?

85
04:44.494 --> 04:45.619
- Make it quick. - Yes, sir!

86
04:45.619 --> 04:47.513
- Thank you! - Let's go!

87
04:49.849 --> 04:52.119
- Corporal Park Min Seok? - Huh?

88
04:53.089 --> 04:55.087
Oh, as expected of the ace.

89
04:55.087 --> 04:59.569
Didn't you say the youngest should always have coins in their pockets?

90
04:59.569 --> 05:02.669
- Did I teach you such details? - Yes, you did!

91
05:02.669 --> 05:04.596
How are you two so in sync lately?

92
05:04.596 --> 05:07.196
- Oh? We've always been in sync. - That's right!

93
05:07.196 --> 05:08.769
- Boom! Clap! - Clap!

94
05:08.769 --> 05:10.310
It's "Boom," sir!

95
05:10.310 --> 05:14.483
- Look at them. Hurry back. - Yes, sir!

96
05:17.649 --> 05:19.889
- Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

97
05:19.889 --> 05:22.949
- Want some coffee? - I'd love some!

98
05:22.949 --> 05:25.849
- May I go as well? - Go ahead.

99
05:25.849 --> 05:29.158
- We'll be back. Let's go. - Yes, sir!

100
05:33.089 --> 05:35.002
You have coins, right?

101
05:35.002 --> 05:36.769
No, I don't.

102
05:36.769 --> 05:38.789
Me neither.

103
05:38.789 --> 05:40.709
- Let's not go then. - Understood.

104
05:40.709 --> 05:45.589
Hey, hey! Come on! You won't go if you don't have any? Here!

105
05:45.589 --> 05:47.409
- Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! - Go quickly.

106
05:47.409 --> 05:49.049
- Thank you. - Thank you.

107
05:49.049 --> 05:51.549
- Let's go. - Yes, sir.

108
05:51.549 --> 05:53.706
Today's special event!

109
05:58.992 --> 06:00.525
- Corporal Kim Dong Woo! - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

110
06:00.525 --> 06:02.042
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min! - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho!

111
06:02.042 --> 06:06.036
The 2006 Limited Edition thermal liner, the "Yong-kkari!"

112
06:06.036 --> 06:07.714
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min! - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

113
06:07.714 --> 06:09.681
I'll take it!

114
06:09.681 --> 06:15.021
With the warmth of the Yellow Dragon adding +1 to your insulation...

115
06:15.021 --> 06:16.421
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min! - Drum roll!

116
06:16.421 --> 06:17.567
You have to do the drum roll.

117
06:17.567 --> 06:22.473
- Drum roll! - Drum roll!

118
06:22.473 --> 06:26.107
- Jeon Sekai! - Private First Class Jeon Sekai!

119
06:26.107 --> 06:28.989
Oh! May I really have it?

120
06:31.541 --> 06:35.143
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye! Thank you!

121
06:40.007 --> 06:45.221
Wow, it's a royal robe! You look like King Hyeonjong from the drama.

122
06:45.221 --> 06:48.461
Hooray! Hooray!

123
06:48.461 --> 06:51.241
Long live Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

124
06:51.241 --> 06:54.068
Your grace is immeasurable!

125
06:54.068 --> 06:56.037
You're welcome.

126
06:56.959 --> 06:59.294
Does it look good on me?

127
06:59.294 --> 07:01.901
It's annoying how well it suits you.

128
07:01.901 --> 07:04.421
I'm so envious, Your Majesty.

129
07:04.421 --> 07:08.847
I shall treat everyone to the PX today.

130
07:09.646 --> 07:11.541
Thank you!

131
07:11.541 --> 07:13.506
Next is my turn!

132
07:17.061 --> 07:18.827
It's...

133
07:20.741 --> 07:22.402
This!

134
07:24.581 --> 07:26.793
The owner of these cleats is...

135
07:26.793 --> 07:28.907
- Kim Dong Woo! - Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

136
07:28.907 --> 07:32.081
Sergeant Cha Hoon already gave me a pair, so I'm okay.

137
07:32.081 --> 07:34.021
Really?

138
07:34.021 --> 07:35.461
I'm fine too!

139
07:35.461 --> 07:38.333
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu gave me some... - I'm not giving it to you!

140
07:38.333 --> 07:40.335
Ji Jeong Min!

141
07:40.335 --> 07:42.841
If I have those cleats, I'll have to play soccer on the weekend.

142
07:42.841 --> 07:44.292
I'm good.

143
07:44.292 --> 07:46.918
Then, Jeon Se Gye!

144
07:46.918 --> 07:48.635
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

145
07:48.635 --> 07:52.516
I already got the liner, so I'll let someone else have them.

146
07:52.516 --> 07:55.161
These have amazing grip, though.

147
07:55.161 --> 07:57.961
- Then... I'll give them to Park Min Seok? - Thank you!

148
07:57.961 --> 07:59.001
Here.

149
07:59.001 --> 08:02.315
Next up is this!

150
08:02.315 --> 08:03.358
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min! - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho!

151
08:03.358 --> 08:05.371
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

152
08:05.371 --> 08:07.881
- Just give me the helmet! The helmet! - You already got the thermal liner!

153
08:07.881 --> 08:09.961
- Hey, that's different! - Hey, you want a piece of this?

154
08:09.961 --> 08:12.387
"Would you like a bowl of this?"

155
08:13.091 --> 08:15.225
Geez, are you guys that happy?

156
08:15.225 --> 08:17.801
You can't even take those home. What's so great about them?

157
08:17.801 --> 08:19.221
They're much more cushioned.

158
08:19.221 --> 08:22.601
My old helmet smelled like rotten eggs.

159
08:22.601 --> 08:24.471
I still have a long way until discharge.

160
08:24.471 --> 08:25.661
This makes me feel proud.

161
08:25.661 --> 08:28.161
Oh, right!

162
08:28.161 --> 08:32.631
We actually prepared something else.

163
08:36.421 --> 08:40.441
- We still have time left, though. - It's not a discharge beating.

164
08:40.441 --> 08:43.284
- Then what is it? - It is...

165
08:43.284 --> 08:47.982
Drum roll...

166
08:51.601 --> 08:54.117
- Hello, sir. - Welcome.

167
08:54.117 --> 08:56.925
We have to get back before the First Sergeant returns, so hurry up.

168
08:56.925 --> 08:58.421
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

169
08:58.421 --> 09:00.158
Chungseong! Love you!

170
09:00.158 --> 09:03.200
- Hello. - Hello.

171
09:04.002 --> 09:06.991
Hey, this isn't it, right? Huh?

172
09:08.041 --> 09:11.261
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok! How do you like this one?

173
09:11.261 --> 09:16.114
- I wanted to get you this for the CSAT. - Is that a pheasant?

174
09:16.114 --> 09:19.721
- I'd die of embarrassment before the exam. - The real one is over here.

175
09:19.721 --> 09:21.255
Sekai.

176
09:24.397 --> 09:28.375
Here it is. Congratulations!

177
09:28.375 --> 09:29.390
[Chungseong! Love you!]

178
09:29.390 --> 09:30.582
[Kang Chan Seok, Choi Byeong Nam]

179
09:30.582 --> 09:32.298
[Kim Dong Woo, Ji Jeong Min, Cha Byeong Ho, Jeon Se Gye]

180
09:33.166 --> 09:35.568
[Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, 3rd Squad, 2nd Company, 7th Battalion, 45th Regiment, 95th Infantry Division]

181
09:35.568 --> 09:37.981
[Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam, 3rd Squad, 2nd Company, 7th Battalion, 45th Regiment, 95th Infantry Division]

182
09:37.981 --> 09:40.105
Why don't you try it on?

183
09:46.821 --> 09:49.661
[A few days ago] Sir... I'm really begging you...

184
09:49.661 --> 09:52.050
I told you, I'm backed up.

185
09:52.050 --> 09:53.510
Do you know how many kids are getting discharged?

186
09:53.510 --> 09:57.641
They're seniors we really respect and love, so we really want to do this for them...

187
09:57.641 --> 10:00.861
Then you should've come earlier. I have dozens of orders pending.

188
10:00.861 --> 10:02.661
I know, sir... but...

189
10:02.661 --> 10:04.821
We didn't know it would take this long.

190
10:04.821 --> 10:07.730
Please, we'll pay you...

191
10:07.730 --> 10:08.766
double!

192
10:08.766 --> 10:09.921
I'm busy, just go.

193
10:09.921 --> 10:12.107
Sir, isn't there any way?

194
10:12.107 --> 10:14.721
I said no.

195
10:14.721 --> 10:16.378
Sir...

196
10:21.621 --> 10:24.001
Is there really no way?

197
10:24.001 --> 10:26.561
Huh? Wait, where have I seen you before?

198
10:26.561 --> 10:29.325
Do you perhaps recognize me?

199
10:29.325 --> 10:32.966
That's right! Goryeo War! You're Hyeonjong!

200
10:32.966 --> 10:34.782
Yes! That is correct.

201
10:34.782 --> 10:36.512
[Jeon Se Gye]

202
10:36.512 --> 10:40.515
Right, Jeon Se Gye. I knew I'd seen you somewhere before.

203
10:40.515 --> 10:42.997
I really enjoyed that drama.

204
10:42.997 --> 10:45.741
- Why aren't you in any new dramas? - I...

205
10:45.741 --> 10:49.061
Ah, you're in the army now. Silly me.

206
10:49.061 --> 10:52.110
Wow, I'm actually meeting King Hyeonjong.

207
10:52.110 --> 10:53.653
Sir,

208
10:53.653 --> 10:58.900
could you not do it even by royal decree?

209
10:59.781 --> 11:01.623
In that case...

210
11:05.540 --> 11:08.959
Oh, Hyeonjong... A king is a king.

211
11:08.959 --> 11:10.841
You must've been a good senior.

212
11:10.841 --> 11:13.089
Your juniors made such a fuss about it.

213
11:13.089 --> 11:16.038
Since they're doing me a favor, I couldn't say no.

214
11:16.038 --> 11:19.005
- Thank you! - Our Se Gye has still got it, huh?

215
11:19.005 --> 11:24.248
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye! I still have it!

216
11:24.248 --> 11:27.794
- Long live Your Majesty! - Long live Your Majesty!

217
11:27.794 --> 11:30.469
May you be discharged.

218
11:31.984 --> 11:36.071
- This must've cost a lot. - We can't go to the PX for a while.

219
11:36.071 --> 11:39.001
Attention, personnel from Barracks 1 and 3,

220
11:39.001 --> 11:42.035
please gather in the multipurpose room.

221
11:44.037 --> 11:46.170
- Kim Sang Hun. - Oh, Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

222
11:46.170 --> 11:48.701
Is the Company Commander planning a surprise for our discharge?

223
11:48.701 --> 11:53.153
- He doesn't have to do that. - I know you love it.

224
11:54.173 --> 11:56.049
- Is everyone here? - Yes, sir!

225
11:56.049 --> 11:57.258
Sit down.

226
11:57.258 --> 11:59.621
- Are Chan Seok and Byeong Nam here? - Yes, sir.

227
11:59.621 --> 12:01.701
Why haven't you guys gone home yet?

228
12:01.701 --> 12:03.531
We don't have much time left.

229
12:03.531 --> 12:07.021
You might miss us, so please be nice.

230
12:07.021 --> 12:10.989
- Kids, aren't you jealous they're going home? - Yes, sir!

231
12:10.989 --> 12:16.069
Don't be jealous. We're going to training, not home.

232
12:16.069 --> 12:17.101
Training?

233
12:17.101 --> 12:18.403
All of a sudden?

234
12:18.403 --> 12:20.275
Yes! Hoguk Exercise!

235
12:20.275 --> 12:22.275
- Hoguk Exercise... - When is it?

236
12:22.275 --> 12:24.489
In four days!

237
12:24.489 --> 12:27.925
It's a joint exercise, so it'll be a good experience.

238
12:27.925 --> 12:29.040
Better than going home, right?

239
12:29.040 --> 12:30.364
Yes, sir!

240
12:30.364 --> 12:32.629
Hoguk Exercise is the best training.

241
12:32.629 --> 12:35.829
Too bad I can't go, even if I wanted to.

242
12:35.829 --> 12:39.968
Now, here's the part that'll really excite you!

243
12:39.968 --> 12:45.729
For this training, the 2nd Company has been given a very special mission!

244
12:45.729 --> 12:49.014
You'll be the opposing force!

245
12:49.014 --> 12:50.019
Opposing force?

246
12:50.019 --> 12:51.969
- We're the opposing force? - Yes!

247
12:51.969 --> 12:55.049
Isn't that usually for tough guys like the Special Forces?

248
12:55.049 --> 12:58.309
- Can he even be the opposing force? - I can... I can be a human shield.

249
12:58.309 --> 13:01.369
- What's the opposing force? - It's something very exhausting.

250
13:01.369 --> 13:04.969
It doesn't make sense for regular infantry to be the opposing force.

251
13:04.969 --> 13:07.912
Quiet, quiet. You're surprised, right?

252
13:07.912 --> 13:09.729
I was very surprised at first, too!

253
13:09.729 --> 13:12.369
But they don't just pick anyone.

254
13:12.369 --> 13:15.920
The 2nd Company has always done well, and among them,

255
13:15.920 --> 13:19.892
Barracks 1 and Barracks 3 were judged to be the best in terms of proficiency and teamwork.

256
13:19.892 --> 13:24.129
That's why you were specially selected.

257
13:24.129 --> 13:26.089
Is it because one of us is the division commander's son?

258
13:26.089 --> 13:29.209
- No comment! - I'm sure that's not it!

259
13:29.209 --> 13:32.849
- Feeling the pressure? - Honestly, it's a lot of pressure.

260
13:32.849 --> 13:35.552
- Im Da Hye, hit the deck. - Hit the deck!

261
13:35.552 --> 13:39.029
- No, no. Sit back down. - Yes, sir. Sorry, sir.

262
13:39.029 --> 13:42.606
With your skills,

263
13:42.606 --> 13:48.466
I believe you can complete this mission successfully.

264
13:49.775 --> 13:52.259
I believe in you, but just in case,

265
13:52.259 --> 13:55.809
train hard until then! With confidence!

266
13:55.809 --> 13:59.797
- Let's prepare well. Got it? - Yes, sir!

267
13:59.797 --> 14:01.132
Look at you guys.

268
14:01.132 --> 14:05.809
Listen, not everyone can be the opposing force.

269
14:05.809 --> 14:10.569
It's a mission only for Korea's elite. Do you know what that means?

270
14:10.569 --> 14:14.589
It means you are Korea's elite!

271
14:14.589 --> 14:16.429
- Do you understand? - Yes, sir!

272
14:16.429 --> 14:19.869
- Good! Louder and with confidence, okay? - Yes, sir!

273
14:19.869 --> 14:23.780
- Right! Keep that momentum going, okay? - Yes, sir!

274
14:23.780 --> 14:25.490
This was decided in a hurry,

275
14:25.490 --> 14:29.829
so those with scheduled leave can still go.

276
14:29.829 --> 14:31.647
Was Hyeon Uk the next one on leave?

277
14:31.647 --> 14:34.149
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Yes, sir.

278
14:34.149 --> 14:35.853
- Lucky you. - I'm so jealous.

279
14:35.853 --> 14:38.836
- Lucky? - I really want to go to the training.

280
14:38.836 --> 14:41.089
- Jeon Se Gye! - Private First Class Jeon Sekai!

281
14:41.089 --> 14:44.569
The Ministry of Defense requested your dispatch, so get ready.

282
14:44.569 --> 14:46.136
Huh?

283
14:46.136 --> 14:48.583
Then what about the training?

284
14:48.583 --> 14:50.073
You're exempt.

285
14:50.848 --> 14:53.478
Sir, I want to participate in the training.

286
14:53.478 --> 14:54.929
The official orders are already out.

287
14:54.929 --> 14:57.449
I'm really disappointed.

288
14:57.449 --> 14:58.509
- Stop lying. - Stop lying.

289
14:58.509 --> 15:00.776
And Chan Seok and Byeong Nam.

290
15:00.776 --> 15:03.149
- Civilian-to-be Choi Byeong Nam! - Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!

291
15:03.149 --> 15:06.655
No one will be here when you leave. Want to join the training instead?

292
15:06.655 --> 15:10.809
- That sounds good. - Hey, don't say such scary things.

293
15:10.809 --> 15:14.709
Right. While preparing for training, let's get these two ready to go home.

294
15:14.709 --> 15:16.389
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

295
15:16.389 --> 15:17.569
Dismissed.

296
15:17.569 --> 15:20.069
- Wait, sir! I have a question! - What?

297
15:20.069 --> 15:21.969
If we do well in this training,

298
15:21.969 --> 15:25.229
will it be of any help to you, sir?

299
15:25.229 --> 15:29.009
I'm doing it because it's an order,

300
15:29.009 --> 15:33.629
but if you guys do well, I'm sure it will.

301
15:33.629 --> 15:37.969
- Then let's give it our all! - Yes! We'll work hard!

302
15:37.969 --> 15:40.066
- Right, thanks. - Good luck, sir!

303
15:40.066 --> 15:42.082
Good luck, sir!

304
15:42.082 --> 15:44.369
This makes me even more disappointed.

305
15:44.369 --> 15:47.169
- I think I see you smirking. - No, sir.

306
15:47.169 --> 15:49.149
Se Gye, go protect the Ministry of Defense.

307
15:49.149 --> 15:52.712
- Bit Na Ri, won't you protect it too? - I prefer to protect beef soup.

308
15:52.712 --> 15:54.620
- I'll teach you about training before I go. - You guys are so admirable.

309
15:54.620 --> 15:56.623
Grab your notes and gather around.

310
15:56.623 --> 16:00.661
What will we do without the two who look most like the opposing force?

311
16:05.090 --> 16:08.289
Hyeon Uk, you're lucky to go on leave instead of training, right?

312
16:08.289 --> 16:10.349
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! No, sir...

313
16:10.349 --> 16:12.725
I really want to participate in training.

314
16:12.725 --> 16:14.209
Can't I change my leave to another day?

315
16:14.209 --> 16:18.603
You'll have plenty of training later, so just enjoy your leave, man.

316
16:18.603 --> 16:20.094
Yes, sir.

317
16:20.094 --> 16:22.569
Now, since we have to prepare...

318
16:22.569 --> 16:26.389
- Let's get our youngest ready for leave! - Yes, sir!

319
16:26.389 --> 16:28.589
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

320
16:28.589 --> 16:31.042
- Come here. - Yes, sir.

321
16:36.807 --> 16:42.323
Wow, a custom beret from Corporal Im Da Hye, the master of shaping.

322
17:16.469 --> 17:19.408
Have a good trip, son.

323
17:20.165 --> 17:22.905
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Thank you!

324
17:22.905 --> 17:25.243
- Go get your combat boots. - Yes, sir.

325
17:27.829 --> 17:30.069
Min Seok, you ready?

326
17:30.069 --> 17:32.880
Corporal Park Min Seok! Ready!

327
17:38.792 --> 17:40.101
It's your first leave,

328
17:40.101 --> 17:45.106
so don't drink too much and don't get hurt, okay?

329
17:45.106 --> 17:46.689
And if anything happens,

330
17:46.689 --> 17:50.049
call the First Sergeant or the unit. Okay?

331
17:50.049 --> 17:51.764
Yes, sir!

332
17:53.615 --> 17:55.507
You have family at home,

333
17:55.507 --> 17:58.089
but in the military, your comrades are your family.

334
17:58.089 --> 18:01.949
Family is about washing, sleeping,

335
18:01.949 --> 18:05.468
crying, and laughing together as you endure.

336
18:08.421 --> 18:12.885
Thank you all so much!

337
18:17.285 --> 18:19.490
We're done, so let's take a break!

338
18:19.490 --> 18:20.992
Yes, sir!

339
18:24.385 --> 18:26.778
If we go back in, they'll make us work.

340
18:30.345 --> 18:32.685
- Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri? - Yeah?

341
18:32.685 --> 18:35.240
Everyone is taking such good care of me.

342
18:35.240 --> 18:39.745
I'm grateful, but I also feel a bit guilty about it.

343
18:39.745 --> 18:42.205
I felt the same way when I went on my first leave.

344
18:42.205 --> 18:44.579
Let's be really nice to our juniors.

345
18:44.579 --> 18:46.185
Yes, sir.

346
18:46.185 --> 18:50.245
- You're happy to go on leave, right? - To be honest, I feel a bit uneasy.

347
18:50.245 --> 18:51.325
Huh? Why?

348
18:51.325 --> 18:54.245
When I'm gone, the recycling and cleaning of the barracks...

349
18:54.245 --> 18:57.386
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri, you'll have to do it all by yourself.

350
18:57.386 --> 18:59.605
Hey, don't worry. I can handle it.

351
18:59.605 --> 19:02.350
I know, but it's always better when there are two of us.

352
19:02.350 --> 19:05.853
Forget it. Don't worry about me. Go have fun.

353
19:05.853 --> 19:07.165
Time flies, you know?

354
19:07.165 --> 19:10.365
On your first leave, did you spend time with your friends?

355
19:10.365 --> 19:12.585
Or did you spend it with your parents?

356
19:12.585 --> 19:15.905
I spent the whole time with my dad.

357
19:15.905 --> 19:18.131
My mother isn't around.

358
19:18.925 --> 19:22.945
- I'm sorry... - And I don't have many close friends.

359
19:22.945 --> 19:27.765
- I'm sorry about that too. - Why? You didn't know. It's okay.

360
19:27.765 --> 19:31.245
Your parents must be so happy to see you when you go home.

361
19:31.245 --> 19:34.015
I think my mother will be very happy.

362
19:34.015 --> 19:36.055
Oh, I don't have a father.

363
19:36.718 --> 19:40.125
- I'm sorry... - It's okay!

364
19:40.125 --> 19:42.283
We have a lot in common.

365
19:42.283 --> 19:44.020
Even our looks.

366
19:44.745 --> 19:45.936
Come again?

367
19:45.936 --> 19:49.585
- I'm kidding. Why so serious? - I'm sorry.

368
19:49.585 --> 19:51.385
- Hey, focus! - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

369
19:51.385 --> 19:54.111
- Look at you! - I'm sorry!

370
19:54.111 --> 19:57.364
When you're out, spend a lot of time with your mom.

371
19:57.364 --> 19:59.965
- Don't just go out meeting girls. - I'm not like that.

372
19:59.965 --> 20:02.225
I'm not saying this because I'm jealous.

373
20:02.225 --> 20:06.707
- Really? - Okay, I'm a little jealous. Happy?

374
20:06.707 --> 20:11.545
When you become the senior, I'll definitely plan a visit for you!

375
20:11.545 --> 20:14.782
- Really? - One hundred percent!

376
20:17.725 --> 20:20.416
- Is that a promise? - I swear!

377
20:21.385 --> 20:23.205
- I just can't hate you. - Thank you!

378
20:23.205 --> 20:26.245
- I'll treat you to the PX when you're back! - Thank you!

379
20:26.245 --> 20:28.876
- Let's head back in. - Yes, sir!

380
20:29.925 --> 20:32.824
- Hurry up. - Yes, sir!

381
20:35.085 --> 20:37.965
I think this guy is acting.

382
20:37.965 --> 20:40.785
No, sir. I'm truly sad to leave.

383
20:40.785 --> 20:42.910
I think I saw your mouth twitching...

384
20:42.910 --> 20:46.321
My nickname is Smile Angel, so I smile naturally.

385
20:46.321 --> 20:48.125
Your eyes look like they're smiling too.

386
20:48.125 --> 20:52.905
I just have a smiley face. I'm really sad.

387
20:52.905 --> 20:54.788
Give it a rest.

388
20:56.237 --> 20:59.191
He's such a good actor, I can't tell what's real.

389
20:59.191 --> 21:01.845
It's real. Please believe me.

390
21:01.845 --> 21:06.098
Then I won't be here to see Sergeants Kang Chan Seok and Choi Byeong Nam leave?

391
21:06.098 --> 21:07.270
I guess not.

392
21:07.270 --> 21:08.905
What if no one is there to see you off?

393
21:08.905 --> 21:11.725
I wanted to see you go... It's a shame.

394
21:11.725 --> 21:14.225
Can't you wait until we get back?

395
21:14.225 --> 21:18.111
Wait for what? Don't talk nonsense.

396
21:18.111 --> 21:20.945
I'll walk out quietly holding Chan Seok's hand, so don't worry.

397
21:20.945 --> 21:23.865
Yeah, I didn't think of that.

398
21:23.865 --> 21:26.578
I imagined you guys standing there when I left for home...

399
21:26.578 --> 21:30.375
And saying, "Good job, Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!"

400
21:30.375 --> 21:31.965
It's a real shame...

401
21:31.965 --> 21:34.949
We can say our goodbyes before that.

402
21:35.753 --> 21:37.783
Let's go for a smoke break.

403
21:43.185 --> 21:45.436
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok?

404
21:45.436 --> 21:47.962
Hey, Se Gye.

405
21:48.785 --> 21:50.545
Here.

406
21:50.545 --> 21:52.180
What is it?

407
21:52.180 --> 21:55.079
This is my contact info for outside.

408
21:55.792 --> 21:56.805
Contact info?

409
21:56.805 --> 22:01.612
In case our schedules don't match and I can't see you two off.

410
22:01.612 --> 22:05.055
I'd love to see you again.

411
22:05.055 --> 22:07.116
What? Jeon Sekai, where's mine?

412
22:08.134 --> 22:09.448
Unbelievable...

413
22:09.448 --> 22:12.624
I have it! I'm messing around.

414
22:12.624 --> 22:15.785
- Here it is. - You scared me, man.

415
22:15.785 --> 22:19.713
I'll treat you two to a proper meal once I'm out!

416
22:19.713 --> 22:22.656
So please...

417
22:22.656 --> 22:24.688
keep my number!

418
22:25.427 --> 22:27.929
Chungseong! Love you.

419
22:27.929 --> 22:29.425
Thanks.

420
22:31.265 --> 22:33.035
Take care.

421
22:38.725 --> 22:42.685
Thanks to Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, I was able to adjust well.

422
22:42.685 --> 22:48.612
My best senior, Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, I'll definitely see you again!

423
22:48.612 --> 22:50.605
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

424
22:50.605 --> 22:53.688
I hope to see you in the real world too.

425
22:53.688 --> 22:55.375
I'll be waiting for your call.

426
22:55.375 --> 22:58.827
I should call Se Gye "hyung" when I get out, right?

427
23:04.905 --> 23:06.339
Are you that happy?

428
23:06.339 --> 23:08.975
Yeah, I am.

429
23:12.385 --> 23:15.604
You raised your successor well.

430
23:20.882 --> 23:23.885
What are you thinking so hard about?

431
23:23.885 --> 23:26.448
What? Why?

432
23:26.448 --> 23:31.243
You look like a citizen who lost his country, or a soldier whose leave was canceled.

433
23:31.243 --> 23:32.429
Is that so?

434
23:32.429 --> 23:34.165
How's life as an officer?

435
23:34.165 --> 23:37.251
The army being shitty is the same for everyone.

436
23:37.251 --> 23:40.136
I thought it'd be different as an officer.

437
23:40.136 --> 23:42.424
It's not like that at all.

438
23:43.245 --> 23:44.596
Man...

439
23:45.216 --> 23:46.677
Never mind.

440
23:46.677 --> 23:49.970
What is it? I hate it when people stop mid-sentence. Seriously.

441
23:49.970 --> 23:53.507
It's not my problem to worry about,

442
23:53.507 --> 23:56.625
but I'm worried for the Company Commander and the Battalion Commander.

443
23:56.625 --> 23:57.813
Worried about what?

444
23:57.813 --> 24:00.018
Company Commander is up for his last promotion.

445
24:00.018 --> 24:03.438
Battalion Commander is being watched by the higher-ups.

446
24:03.438 --> 24:06.695
Is it right to go into such a big training so suddenly like this?

447
24:06.695 --> 24:08.238
That's the army for you.

448
24:08.238 --> 24:11.625
Battalion Commander is so good, would the higher-ups leave him alone?

449
24:11.625 --> 24:13.619
I just feel bad for the Company Commander.

450
24:13.619 --> 24:16.790
He's exactly what the army needs.

451
24:16.790 --> 24:18.865
He'll definitely get promoted.

452
24:18.865 --> 24:21.017
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu? - What?

453
24:21.017 --> 24:24.017
- You're back to your old self. - What is?

454
24:24.017 --> 24:27.973
Complaining and grumbling, that's the real Choi Il Gu.

455
24:28.856 --> 24:32.083
It's reassuring to have you guys at a time like this.

456
24:32.083 --> 24:33.599
How much time do you have left?

457
24:33.599 --> 24:36.579
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam! Five days left.

458
24:36.579 --> 24:38.017
How does it feel to be getting out soon?

459
24:38.017 --> 24:41.117
Why even ask? It feels great, of course.

460
24:41.117 --> 24:44.735
Everyone says it's bittersweet, and it really is.

461
24:44.735 --> 24:47.528
Prepare well before you leave.

462
24:47.528 --> 24:48.777
Prepare for what?

463
24:48.777 --> 24:52.737
I thought I could do anything once I got out of here.

464
24:52.737 --> 24:56.705
But I should've prepared to be damn good at everything before leaving.

465
24:56.705 --> 25:02.626
Chan Seok is doing a great job! What about you? What will you do?

466
25:02.626 --> 25:04.378
Me?

467
25:04.378 --> 25:06.617
I'll just go back to school and look for a job.

468
25:06.617 --> 25:08.717
Job hunting is tough, too.

469
25:08.717 --> 25:13.637
- Is that why you signed on for more? - Hey!

470
25:13.637 --> 25:16.877
Hey, take everything you can from here.

471
25:16.877 --> 25:20.217
- You still won't tell me? - You bastard!

472
25:20.217 --> 25:21.813
You don't know anything.

473
25:21.813 --> 25:26.037
If I were you, I'd have done the last training before leaving.

474
25:26.037 --> 25:28.797
Don't make such creepy jokes.

475
25:28.797 --> 25:32.517
Now that it's over, that's my biggest regret.

476
25:32.517 --> 25:37.621
I should've done everything I could for myself and the guys before leaving...

477
25:37.621 --> 25:40.237
You guys don't have much time left,

478
25:40.237 --> 25:42.000
but try to leave with fewer regrets.

479
25:42.000 --> 25:45.537
Oh, my. You've really grown up, haven't you?

480
25:45.537 --> 25:48.379
I've always been an adult, you bastard.

481
25:48.379 --> 25:51.197
- I'm leaving first. - Where are you going?

482
25:51.197 --> 25:53.257
Company Commander must be feeling restless.

483
25:53.257 --> 25:56.388
He's having a drink, and he wants me there.

484
25:56.388 --> 25:57.641
Can I go with you?

485
25:57.641 --> 25:59.608
Desert and come with me then.

486
25:59.608 --> 26:02.037
I was just kidding.

487
26:02.037 --> 26:03.312
Enjoy your drink.

488
26:03.312 --> 26:04.898
Chungseong! Love you!

489
26:04.898 --> 26:07.709
- What's with the salute? Are you sick? - Right?

490
26:07.709 --> 26:09.807
It felt awkward for me too.

491
26:13.266 --> 26:17.557
Brother! No! You have to come with us! You said we'd get out alive!

492
26:17.557 --> 26:21.057
Go! If you don't want to die! Your mother is waiting for you!

493
26:21.057 --> 26:24.488
You have to live for me to live! Go!

494
26:31.507 --> 26:34.603
- Brother, wake up! Please! - Jae Hoon...

495
26:34.603 --> 26:37.997
Brother! Speak to me! I'm here!

496
26:37.997 --> 26:41.615
Take care of Mother...

497
26:42.906 --> 26:45.624
Brother, don't die!

498
26:45.624 --> 26:50.301
If you die, how am I supposed to live? Don't leave me...

499
26:50.301 --> 26:53.030
- No! - We have to run!

500
26:53.030 --> 26:57.721
- Let go! - Jae Hoon, you must survive...

501
27:01.908 --> 27:05.061
[The Flag Flutters]

502
27:06.543 --> 27:08.837
This is the duty officer.

503
27:09.737 --> 27:12.017
As of this moment, all personnel...

504
27:12.017 --> 27:14.519
Prepare to write your wills. That is all.

505
27:15.687 --> 27:18.197
A... a will? You mean a will?

506
27:18.197 --> 27:20.477
- Min Seok, is this your first time too? - Yes.

507
27:20.477 --> 27:23.539
Sometimes we write them before big drills.

508
27:23.539 --> 27:25.185
I'm actually a bit scared.

509
27:25.185 --> 27:27.254
It feels a bit strange.

510
27:27.254 --> 27:29.483
Put some hair and nails in, too.

511
27:29.483 --> 27:31.250
Are you serious?

512
27:31.250 --> 27:32.917
I'm serious, man.

513
27:32.917 --> 27:36.183
- Get ready. - Yes, sir.

514
27:38.717 --> 27:41.297
Wait, we're not even doing the drill, so we don't have to write one, right?

515
27:41.297 --> 27:45.816
- Just write it. When else will you do this? - That's true.

516
27:47.402 --> 27:51.987
- Dear... - Dear Mother and Father.

517
27:52.957 --> 27:55.177
Mother, Father, how are you?

518
27:55.177 --> 27:58.617
I've always been a man of few words, giving only short answers at home,

519
27:58.617 --> 28:00.917
and it weighs on me that I was so blunt.

520
28:00.917 --> 28:05.557
Today, the admin office gave us paper to write our wills before the drill.

521
28:05.557 --> 28:09.037
I am heading to the battlefield to fulfill my duty as a soldier.

522
28:09.037 --> 28:11.917
I wonder if I've only caused my mother more heartache.

523
28:11.917 --> 28:14.897
If you read this, I'm worried you'll cry all night.

524
28:14.897 --> 28:18.717
If you're reading this, it means something bad has happened to me.

525
28:18.717 --> 28:24.477
With my seniors and juniors in the same unit, I'm not afraid even in a time of war.

526
28:24.477 --> 28:28.625
Since this is a step forward as a soldier protecting our country,

527
28:28.625 --> 28:32.421
please don't be sad and stay healthy.

528
28:33.589 --> 28:38.237
Thank you for raising me with such love.

529
28:38.237 --> 28:40.877
I'll be a son you can be proud of until the end.

530
28:40.877 --> 28:44.557
Thank you for giving birth to me and raising me.

531
28:44.557 --> 28:47.037
I miss you. I love you, Dad.

532
28:47.037 --> 28:50.817
Mom, Dad. I love you so much.

533
28:50.817 --> 28:52.677
Please stay healthy.

534
28:52.677 --> 28:58.677
This Hoguk Exercise is not a joint exercise with the US military, but a solo Korean drill.

535
28:58.677 --> 29:02.289
It's a large-scale drill involving the Marine Corps,

536
29:02.289 --> 29:04.917
Army, Navy, and Air Force.

537
29:04.917 --> 29:10.037
A drop of sweat in training replaces a drop of blood in battle.

538
29:10.037 --> 29:13.877
What if a real situation breaks out tonight?

539
29:13.877 --> 29:16.806
Or what if you're found as a cold corpse

540
29:16.806 --> 29:20.057
due to an accident during training?

541
29:20.057 --> 29:22.497
What will be sent back to your parents?

542
29:22.497 --> 29:25.837
The fingernails and hair in this ziplock bag...

543
29:25.837 --> 29:30.937
and that single piece of paper in your hand.

544
29:30.937 --> 29:32.217
Though it's just a piece of paper,

545
29:32.217 --> 29:37.985
it's your final goodbye and a message of love

546
29:37.985 --> 29:40.295
to those you care about.

547
29:40.295 --> 29:43.657
It's the last message you can send them.

548
29:43.657 --> 29:47.537
Though it's a drill, act as if you're heading to a real battlefield.

549
29:47.537 --> 29:50.183
For the sake of those who will see this,

550
29:50.183 --> 29:53.518
I hope you write your final goodbye

551
29:53.518 --> 29:56.228
with all your heart. That's all.

552
30:20.946 --> 30:22.713
Corporal Cha Byeong Ho!

553
30:24.297 --> 30:26.298
Corporal Ji Jeong Min!

554
30:28.513 --> 30:30.664
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!

555
30:32.213 --> 30:34.108
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

556
30:36.009 --> 30:37.919
Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

557
30:39.873 --> 30:42.192
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

558
30:48.153 --> 30:51.053
I got so immersed in writing my will that I almost cried.

559
30:51.053 --> 30:54.913
I thought of my mom and dad, and it felt strange.

560
30:54.913 --> 31:00.373
It's a shame Sergeant Kang Chan Seok and Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam aren't here.

561
31:00.373 --> 31:03.403
It's a shame, but it can't be helped.

562
31:03.403 --> 31:05.482
It really is a shame.

563
31:05.482 --> 31:06.993
It would've been nice if Se Gye could go too.

564
31:06.993 --> 31:10.533
- That's a shame too. - I'm really disappointed as well.

565
31:10.533 --> 31:14.568
- I want to go... - You'll have plenty of chances later.

566
31:14.568 --> 31:17.020
Yes, sir.

567
31:17.633 --> 31:19.880
- Lights out. - Good night, sir.

568
31:19.880 --> 31:22.958
- Love you! - Love you. Good night.

569
31:26.833 --> 31:28.741
Good night, sir.

570
31:50.933 --> 31:53.080
- Chungseong! Love you! - That was a nice speech.

571
31:53.080 --> 31:55.013
- Come again, sir? - Never mind if you didn't hear it.

572
31:55.013 --> 31:57.863
- Was it something good? - No.

573
31:58.853 --> 32:04.032
- Were there any kids messing around? - No, sir. Everyone was very serious.

574
32:06.133 --> 32:07.773
But why are you putting stamps on them?

575
32:07.773 --> 32:11.898
I thought the parents would appreciate seeing these!

576
32:13.373 --> 32:16.673
- You're sending these home? - Yes, sir! That's right!

577
32:16.673 --> 32:21.923
Wouldn't they be happy to see the resolve and filial piety of the sons they raised?

578
32:21.923 --> 32:24.133
The unit will be in total chaos if they see this.

579
32:24.133 --> 32:29.073
For example, we'll be bombarded with calls asking if their sons are going to die.

580
32:29.073 --> 32:32.953
Then Army Headquarters will find out, and they'll send the Military Police.

581
32:32.953 --> 32:35.065
Battalion Commander and I will be hauled off,

582
32:35.065 --> 32:38.791
and you'll be forcibly discharged.

583
32:40.617 --> 32:41.937
Fine!

584
32:42.622 --> 32:44.798
Write your will.

585
32:44.798 --> 32:46.913
- A... a will, sir? - Yes.

586
32:46.913 --> 32:52.153
If I take that to mean I might die at the hands of the Company Commander...

587
32:52.153 --> 32:54.095
You two, freeze.

588
33:02.493 --> 33:06.693
Chungseong! Love you! Sergeant Kang Chan Seok and one other.

589
33:06.693 --> 33:10.973
Our seniors can't sleep? What brings you to the admin office?

590
33:10.973 --> 33:12.664
We're here to...

591
33:18.093 --> 33:21.493
We're here to apply for a discharge delay!

592
33:28.590 --> 33:30.853
Did I hear that right?

593
33:30.853 --> 33:33.680
I think you did, sir.

594
33:33.680 --> 33:37.834
You were so desperate to go home. Why the sudden change of heart?

595
33:37.834 --> 33:39.251
It's...

596
33:40.693 --> 33:43.665
It's just that when I lay down to sleep...

597
33:53.093 --> 33:58.598
I kept thinking about what I wrote in my will, and I couldn't sleep.

598
33:58.598 --> 34:03.121
Dear parents, this is Chan Seok.

599
34:04.113 --> 34:09.389
I'm writing this thinking that it might be my last letter.

600
34:10.090 --> 34:11.988
You bastard, behave yourself!

601
34:11.988 --> 34:13.428
Give me some snacks.

602
34:13.428 --> 34:19.099
Thank you for raising a son who was always a troublemaker with love.

603
34:19.099 --> 34:23.010
And I'm sorry,

604
34:23.010 --> 34:25.946
but I think I'm going to be a troublesome son once again.

605
34:26.753 --> 34:30.420
The discharge I've been waiting for is finally approaching...

606
34:31.069 --> 34:34.661
But I feel uneasy leaving

607
34:34.661 --> 34:37.409
without having done anything for my juniors.

608
34:37.409 --> 34:38.660
Thinking back,

609
34:38.660 --> 34:42.747
I had seniors who supported me and forgave me when I made mistakes...

610
34:42.747 --> 34:46.001
And seniors who reprimanded me when I did something wrong.

611
34:46.001 --> 34:48.813
That's how I became who I am today.

612
34:48.813 --> 34:54.513
But was I that kind of senior to my juniors?

613
34:54.513 --> 34:58.613
In hindsight, that's my biggest regret... For myself and for the guys.

614
34:58.613 --> 35:01.073
I should've done everything I could.

615
35:01.073 --> 35:05.034
Don't accidents happen sometimes during the opposing force mission?

616
35:05.034 --> 35:06.633
I've never done that kind of training...

617
35:06.633 --> 35:09.553
Don't worry. You'll do fine once you're out there.

618
35:09.553 --> 35:12.679
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

619
35:13.653 --> 35:18.453
I think this is my last chance to be remembered as that kind of senior.

620
35:18.453 --> 35:21.673
So I'm going to be a bad son once more.

621
35:21.673 --> 35:25.876
I'll return safely and share the joy of my discharge with you.

622
35:25.876 --> 35:29.381
I'll come home as a son you can be proud of.

623
35:30.547 --> 35:35.148
From your son Chan Seok, who loves you more than anyone.

624
35:35.928 --> 35:38.068
That guy is coming too...

625
35:44.673 --> 35:46.329
Choi Byeong Nam...

626
35:47.593 --> 35:49.272
Choi Byeong Nam!

627
35:50.231 --> 35:53.108
What? Did you have a nightmare?

628
35:53.108 --> 35:54.876
Let's talk for a second.

629
35:56.433 --> 36:01.013
I really, really, really don't think this is right.

630
36:01.013 --> 36:04.788
I'll get you the latest phone for cheap once I'm out.

631
36:04.788 --> 36:06.532
Still, no.

632
36:06.532 --> 36:09.753
Think about the kids. What about Kim Dong Woo?

633
36:09.753 --> 36:11.062
He's becoming a Sergeant the day after tomorrow.

634
36:11.062 --> 36:13.421
- What about Ji Jeong Min, your favorite? - I don't even like him that much.

635
36:13.421 --> 36:14.925
What about Cha Byeong Ho, who you work out with every day?

636
36:14.925 --> 36:16.873
He was always an ace anyway.

637
36:16.873 --> 36:19.591
Then what about our company commander...

638
36:19.591 --> 36:24.201
- I don't know. - What if the kids get hurt?

639
36:36.301 --> 36:38.699
This unit made me a better person,

640
36:38.699 --> 36:41.821
and I wanted to help my fellow soldiers one last time before I leave.

641
36:41.821 --> 36:45.341
Oh! Choi Byeong Nam is joining too.

642
36:45.341 --> 36:49.999
That's right. I just woke up, so my face is like this,

643
36:49.999 --> 36:52.022
but I volunteered.

644
36:53.681 --> 36:57.050
Wow... I'm so proud of you guys!

645
36:57.050 --> 36:59.803
- Thank you, Chan Seok. - Sergeant Kang Chan Seok.

646
36:59.803 --> 37:01.625
- Byeong Nam. - Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

647
37:01.625 --> 37:02.637
I'm truly moved.

648
37:02.637 --> 37:04.381
- You guys are really cool. - Get lost.

649
37:04.381 --> 37:07.938
- I'll remember your dedication! - I'm so touched...

650
37:07.938 --> 37:10.554
You're so admirable.

651
37:12.661 --> 37:14.292
To participate in the Hoguk Exercise,

652
37:14.292 --> 37:16.776
a round of applause

653
37:16.776 --> 37:21.411
for Sergeants Kang Chan Seok and Choi Byeong Nam!

654
37:23.180 --> 37:25.326
You guys are awesome!

655
37:27.414 --> 37:29.958
- True soldiers! True soldiers! - So cool.

656
37:29.958 --> 37:32.586
- Who's taking the photo? - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo!

657
37:32.586 --> 37:34.794
- Take a good one. - I'll take it now.

658
37:34.794 --> 37:37.382
- Please smile. - Fix your faces!

659
37:37.382 --> 37:40.003
One, two, three!

660
37:40.802 --> 37:44.538
- Chungseong. - Love you!

661
37:45.221 --> 37:46.864
Love you!

662
37:46.864 --> 37:48.458
This is nice.

663
37:50.979 --> 37:53.065
Man, you're crazy.

664
37:53.065 --> 37:56.360
- I'm proud of you. - Congratulations.

665
37:56.360 --> 37:58.893
Choi Byeong Nam... Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

666
38:00.403 --> 38:04.461
[Hoguk Exercise D-3]

667
38:04.461 --> 38:07.911
- Are you crying? - It's the medicated patch, you jerk...

668
38:07.911 --> 38:09.601
You wipe it.

669
38:09.601 --> 38:14.881
Soldiers! As the opposing force, we can do a great job!

670
38:14.881 --> 38:17.297
[Hoguk Exercise D-2] We move according to a strict war scenario.

671
38:17.297 --> 38:19.383
We can never win against these guys in a fight.

672
38:19.383 --> 38:22.101
We must stick together and move as one. Got it?

673
38:22.101 --> 38:23.841
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

674
38:23.841 --> 38:28.863
As the opposing force, we need perfect teamwork rather than perfect fitness.

675
38:28.863 --> 38:30.021
Black.

676
38:30.021 --> 38:33.272
- Yes, sir! - Coordination over individual ability.

677
38:33.272 --> 38:34.690
From the ready shooters,

678
38:34.690 --> 38:35.732
commence firing.

679
38:35.732 --> 38:38.071
- Commence firing! - Commence firing!

680
38:44.425 --> 38:48.470
Covering for each other's weaknesses and being each other's strength.

681
38:49.162 --> 38:52.398
That is the strength of our 2nd Company!

682
38:52.398 --> 38:56.219
[Hoguk Exercise D-1] ♪ Korea's strongest, aim high ♪

683
38:56.219 --> 38:58.466
♪ Aim high ♪

684
38:58.466 --> 39:02.220
[7 hours before Hoguk Exercise]

685
39:12.541 --> 39:15.841
Darn mosquitoes...

686
39:15.841 --> 39:18.901
- Okay. - I lost again...

687
39:18.901 --> 39:20.645
You're no match for me, newbie.

688
39:20.645 --> 39:22.501
Why are you so good at this?

689
39:22.501 --> 39:23.893
You're just bad at it.

690
39:23.893 --> 39:25.701
What... Is bingo all you did?

691
39:25.701 --> 39:28.327
Yeah, I did everything you couldn't.

692
39:28.327 --> 39:30.739
Chungseong! Love you!

693
39:30.739 --> 39:34.122
Yoon Mo, spray some bug spray in every barrack.

694
39:34.122 --> 39:37.878
- Spray a lot in the 3rd barrack. - Yes, sir.

695
39:37.878 --> 39:40.381
I caught Kim Sang Hun again.

696
39:40.381 --> 39:43.036
- Let me check. - Check what?

697
39:58.941 --> 40:01.001
I forgot...

698
40:01.001 --> 40:02.867
- Hey. - Yes?

699
40:02.867 --> 40:04.949
- Sung Yoon Mo. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

700
40:04.949 --> 40:07.209
Do you think I'm a pushover?

701
40:07.209 --> 40:10.522
- No... No, sir. - Why didn't you do what I told you?

702
40:10.522 --> 40:12.461
I told you to go to the supply room.

703
40:12.461 --> 40:16.222
- I forgot... - Give me your palm! You need a beating.

704
40:16.222 --> 40:17.709
Give me your palm!

705
40:17.709 --> 40:20.681
This won't do. I'll use this. Give me your palm.

706
40:20.681 --> 40:22.497
- Stay still! - Cor... Corporal No Hee Jeong?

707
40:22.497 --> 40:24.341
- This is... - It'll hurt. Hold it out.

708
40:24.341 --> 40:26.802
- I'll do better. Please spare me. - Oh, it's like this.

709
40:26.802 --> 40:28.781
It's going to hurt.

710
40:28.781 --> 40:31.272
Please spare me!

711
40:51.493 --> 40:53.187
Huh? What?

712
40:53.187 --> 40:55.301
Don't spray it near my face...

713
40:55.301 --> 40:59.491
- Yes, sir. - Are you brainless?

714
41:46.590 --> 41:49.678
You little brat...

715
41:49.678 --> 41:51.330
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo...

716
41:51.330 --> 41:55.425
Look at this guy...

717
42:02.626 --> 42:05.857
You little... Hey!

718
42:05.857 --> 42:07.819
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo...

719
42:13.221 --> 42:15.641
My eyes sting, so stop spraying.

720
42:15.641 --> 42:18.219
I'm going to die before the mosquitoes.

721
42:18.219 --> 42:20.872
Yes, I'm... I'm sorry.

722
42:20.872 --> 42:23.561
Just spray under my spot one more time before you go.

723
42:23.561 --> 42:25.679
Yes, sir.

724
42:36.803 --> 42:39.881
- Good night. - Good job.

725
42:39.881 --> 42:41.808
Yes, sir.

726
43:01.290 --> 43:03.531
Hey, Moon Bit Na Ri, stay alert.

727
43:03.531 --> 43:05.106
Yes, sir!

728
43:06.470 --> 43:10.705
[Hoguk Exercise D-Day] [Gyeonggi Mountain Training Site]

729
43:11.383 --> 43:14.285
Hey, we're here. Wake up.

730
43:18.307 --> 43:20.581
- Stay alert, everyone. - All right, dismount.

731
43:20.581 --> 43:22.241
- Dismount. - Dismount.

732
43:22.241 --> 43:24.897
- Stay sharp from this moment on. - Yes, sir.

733
43:24.897 --> 43:26.523
Watch your step.

734
43:26.523 --> 43:28.280
Make sure you all get down carefully.

735
43:28.280 --> 43:30.582
Form two lines. No more smiling.

736
43:30.582 --> 43:31.987
- If I see teeth, you're dead. - Prepare for battle!

737
43:31.987 --> 43:35.719
Invincible! Ah!

738
43:35.719 --> 43:38.027
One, two, three.

739
43:45.709 --> 43:47.358
What's that?

740
43:47.358 --> 43:50.211
Good! To battle positions!

741
43:50.211 --> 43:51.674
Invincible!

742
43:57.211 --> 43:58.870
Invincible!

743
44:13.181 --> 44:17.421
What are those guys? Are they even human?

744
44:17.421 --> 44:19.493
They're not human. They're Marines.

745
44:19.493 --> 44:25.246
They look like real soldiers. They're on a different level from us.

746
44:25.246 --> 44:29.161
- Il Gu, manage the men and set up camp. - Yes, sir.

747
44:29.161 --> 44:33.715
- Seok Jin, come check the terrain with me. - Yes, sir!

748
44:33.715 --> 44:36.576
- Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri. - Get your head in the game!

749
44:36.576 --> 44:40.001
Stop staring and unload the gear! Set up the tents! Move it!

750
44:40.001 --> 44:42.343
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

751
44:44.849 --> 44:47.105
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min. - Hey, take this.

752
44:47.105 --> 44:49.898
- Yes. - Corporal Kim, this...

753
44:49.898 --> 44:51.063
Be careful with that.

754
44:51.063 --> 44:52.231
- Moon Bit Na Ri, hurry up. - Yes, sir!

755
44:52.231 --> 44:53.986
- Lift it right. - It's heavy, so be careful.

756
44:53.986 --> 44:56.098
- Keep it symmetrical. - Hurry, hurry.

757
44:56.098 --> 44:57.647
Don't hold it like that!

758
45:01.262 --> 45:03.761
- What are you doing? - Hey.

759
45:03.761 --> 45:07.301
How can you be the opposing force like this? Pick it up, you're embarrassing us.

760
45:07.301 --> 45:09.292
Yes, sir.

761
45:11.355 --> 45:16.181
- Pilseung! - Pil... Uh... Chungseong.

762
45:16.181 --> 45:17.774
Thank you for the hard work coming here.

763
45:17.774 --> 45:21.180
Our Marines have already set up the tents, so you can just unpack your gear.

764
45:21.180 --> 45:25.141
- Really? Good job. - Well then. I'll see you later.

765
45:25.141 --> 45:27.232
Sure, sure.

766
45:27.232 --> 45:29.781
Wow, the tent lines are a work of art.

767
45:29.781 --> 45:33.081
As expected of Marines, the alignment of these tents is no joke.

768
45:33.081 --> 45:37.981
I get it, so stop admiring them. Are you an audience member? Move it!

769
45:37.981 --> 45:40.263
- Yes, sir! - They're already up, so just put the gear in.

770
45:40.263 --> 45:42.477
Yes, sir. Hey, hold it tight.

771
45:42.477 --> 45:44.376
Yes, sir.

772
45:46.701 --> 45:48.798
Pilseung!

773
45:52.211 --> 45:54.901
Pilseung!

774
45:54.901 --> 45:56.587
Private Choi Uk!

775
45:56.587 --> 45:59.666
I would like to know if I may ask Marine Park Cheol Yong for permission

776
45:59.666 --> 46:04.961
to report that the task of setting up the barracks has been completed!

777
46:04.961 --> 46:06.141
[Assey: Marine slang for a recruit] Assey!

778
46:06.141 --> 46:07.301
Private Choi Uk!

779
46:07.301 --> 46:10.101
Are you losing your voice in front of other units?

780
46:10.101 --> 46:13.883
You've completely lost your spirit!

781
46:15.417 --> 46:19.029
Pilseung! I'll do better!

782
46:19.029 --> 46:21.641
- I think he's overacting on purpose. - I know, right?

783
46:21.641 --> 46:23.501
Private Choi! Uk!

784
46:23.501 --> 46:27.287
I would like to know if I may ask for permission to ask

785
46:27.287 --> 46:29.801
if I may take corrective action

786
46:29.801 --> 46:33.601
for forgetting my Marine spirit in front of other units!

787
46:33.601 --> 46:35.251
Permission granted!

788
46:35.251 --> 46:36.729
He's going to rapture his vocal cords.

789
46:36.729 --> 46:39.060
- "Rupture," you idiot. - Rupture.

790
46:40.081 --> 46:41.430
Always keep this in mind, Assey...

791
46:41.430 --> 46:43.303
[Choi Uk]

792
46:43.303 --> 46:48.892
You can forget to breathe, but never forget that you are a Marine.

793
46:48.892 --> 46:52.050
You're not just a private. You're a Marine!

794
46:53.801 --> 46:56.301
Everyone! Attention!

795
46:56.301 --> 46:58.660
- I think he's an officer. - Pilseung!

796
46:58.660 --> 47:00.261
Pilseung!

797
47:00.261 --> 47:03.689
- Hey, is he a sergeant first class? - I think so.

798
47:08.737 --> 47:11.561
What's with the tent alignment!

799
47:11.561 --> 47:14.042
- Everyone, assemble! - Everyone, assemble!

800
47:14.042 --> 47:17.827
Look at this! You've completely lost your spirit!

801
47:17.827 --> 47:21.550
Marines maintain alignment even in death!

802
47:21.550 --> 47:23.261
- Understood? - Yes!

803
47:23.261 --> 47:28.265
The tent is off by 0.3 centimeters from the Marine regulation margin!

804
47:28.265 --> 47:32.412
- Dismantle it immediately. - Yes, sir!

805
47:35.641 --> 47:37.558
They're tearing it down for 0.3 cm?

806
47:37.558 --> 47:40.149
Wow, that's some crazy charisma...

807
47:40.149 --> 47:42.528
That's a real officer for you...

808
47:42.528 --> 47:43.739
They're actually dismantling it!

809
47:43.739 --> 47:46.376
Crazy bastards...

810
47:47.073 --> 47:49.203
Guys. Let's go help them.

811
47:49.203 --> 47:51.381
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

812
47:52.411 --> 47:55.000
Is there anything we can help with?

813
47:55.000 --> 47:56.681
Excuse me... Marine guys,

814
47:56.681 --> 47:59.141
we'll help you dismantle the tent.

815
47:59.141 --> 48:01.701
How do we do this?

816
48:01.701 --> 48:05.439
- "Guys?" - What the...

817
48:05.439 --> 48:07.281
Yes... Yes?

818
48:07.281 --> 48:09.890
I mean... our guys will help you out.

819
48:09.890 --> 48:13.496
Did you just call a sacred Marine "guy?"

820
48:13.496 --> 48:15.681
What the...

821
48:15.681 --> 48:18.741
Does the Marine Corps look like a bunch of neighborhood guys to you?

822
48:18.741 --> 48:21.191
- These punks... - Hey... don't mess with them.

823
48:21.191 --> 48:24.081
Hey, Cheol Yong. That's enough.

824
48:24.081 --> 48:27.021
Are you showing off your Marine pride just because you're a senior corporal?

825
48:27.021 --> 48:30.361
- Pilseung! I'll do better! - Just manage your subordinates.

826
48:30.361 --> 48:32.409
Yes, sir!

827
48:32.409 --> 48:35.321
I'm sorry. He's a bit intense.

828
48:35.321 --> 48:39.853
Please just call our guys "Marines" instead of "guys."

829
48:39.853 --> 48:41.794
- Marines... - Yes, yes...

830
48:41.794 --> 48:42.950
Yes, sir.

831
48:42.950 --> 48:45.256
- Let's go, Min Seok. - Hurry it up.

832
48:45.256 --> 48:50.305
If it doesn't work, use your grit! Until your teeth break!

833
48:50.305 --> 48:52.128
Will it be okay to share a barracks?

834
48:52.128 --> 48:53.973
We have to show them.

835
48:53.973 --> 48:56.102
Just how scary the Army can be.

836
48:56.102 --> 49:02.109
[Hill 100]

837
49:02.109 --> 49:05.484
Company Commander, according to the manual, this ridge...

838
49:05.484 --> 49:08.496
seems like the optimal spot to build a defensive position.

839
49:08.496 --> 49:09.958
If you look at the rear here...

840
49:09.958 --> 49:11.822
Oh! You scared me!

841
49:11.822 --> 49:14.329
You should watch your step.

842
49:14.329 --> 49:15.607
What is this?

843
49:22.254 --> 49:27.968
[Hill 100]

844
49:27.968 --> 49:31.096
Company Commander, according to the manual, this ridge...

845
49:31.096 --> 49:34.374
seems like the optimal spot to build a defensive position.

846
49:34.374 --> 49:35.833
If you look at the rear here...

847
49:35.833 --> 49:37.561
Oh! You scared me!

848
49:37.561 --> 49:40.230
You should watch your helmet.

849
49:40.230 --> 49:41.586
What is this?

850
49:50.693 --> 49:52.129
A Marine?

851
49:52.129 --> 49:54.369
The training hasn't even started yet...

852
49:54.369 --> 49:56.748
[Pit: A personal trench with a camouflage cover] - Were you digging a pit? - Yes, sir.

853
49:56.748 --> 50:00.653
But are you really planning to build a position here?

854
50:00.653 --> 50:01.957
Well... of course.

855
50:01.957 --> 50:07.573
The dense trees provide great concealment, and the ridge behind ensures survival!

856
50:07.573 --> 50:13.493
The ground is damp here. If you build a position, it'll collapse in no time.

857
50:13.493 --> 50:17.773
Is this "optimal spot" you're talking about actually an optimal spot to die?

858
50:17.773 --> 50:19.673
What?

859
50:19.673 --> 50:21.233
Hey, Marine.

860
50:21.233 --> 50:23.833
Don't you salute officers from other branches?

861
50:23.833 --> 50:28.333
Do you salute the person or the rank? I'm not trying to be rude, but...

862
50:28.333 --> 50:31.028
I'm sorry. Pilseung!

863
50:31.028 --> 50:32.383
Chungseong.

864
50:34.953 --> 50:36.313
Is that guy out of his mind?

865
50:36.313 --> 50:38.664
- Company Commander, let me talk to him. - Sure. Go ahead.

866
50:38.664 --> 50:42.093
- I'm sorry, what was that? - Don't play dumb with me!

867
50:42.093 --> 50:44.053
Don't get caught up in their cocky attitude.

868
50:44.053 --> 50:47.763
- We'll just go at our own pace, okay? - Yes, sir.

869
50:50.233 --> 50:53.884
The ground is pretty damp... They must've trained hard.

870
50:53.884 --> 50:55.456
How reliable!

871
50:56.573 --> 50:58.733
- You're reliable too. - First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

872
50:58.733 --> 51:01.806
- Let's look somewhere else. - Yes, sir.

873
51:11.954 --> 51:14.697
His eyes are like lasers.

874
51:19.933 --> 51:23.846
- Are the soldiers resting well? - Yes, sir!

875
51:24.566 --> 51:28.956
- Those punks, they don't even salute. - I know, right?

876
51:36.292 --> 51:40.917
Everyone, change your clothes!

877
51:43.432 --> 51:49.211
- Hey, if you're sweaty, change. - Yes, sir.

878
52:00.893 --> 52:04.499
Hey, but don't you think we can wear these for one more day?

879
52:04.499 --> 52:06.668
Honestly, we haven't even started training.

880
52:06.668 --> 52:10.853
Right? Yeah... it still feels pretty fresh.

881
52:10.853 --> 52:14.113
- You guys think so too, right? - Yes, sir.

882
52:14.113 --> 52:17.187
What are you saying? You stink. Change.

883
52:17.187 --> 52:18.883
Yes, sir.

884
52:19.733 --> 52:22.837
Hey, Bit Na Ri, why are you taking your clothes off?

885
52:23.953 --> 52:27.133
- I sweated a lot. - No, you didn't.

886
52:27.133 --> 52:30.533
You're ruining the Army's image. Put it on.

887
52:30.533 --> 52:32.667
- I'm sorry! - What's going on?

888
52:32.667 --> 52:35.253
Hey, Bit Na Ri, change. You smell.

889
52:35.253 --> 52:36.922
Yes, sir!

890
52:39.494 --> 52:42.061
Pilseung!

891
52:42.955 --> 52:44.623
Chungseong!

892
52:44.623 --> 52:49.753
Lieutenant, since we'll be comrades from tomorrow, why don't we introduce ourselves?

893
52:49.753 --> 52:53.511
Sure, why not? I'm...

894
52:56.131 --> 52:58.759
Pilseung!

895
52:58.759 --> 53:01.153
I'm Sergeant First Class Ma Tae Ho, Assistant Platoon Leader,

896
53:01.153 --> 53:02.805
Marine Landing Raider Battalion!

897
53:02.805 --> 53:06.511
[Sergeant First Class Ma Tae Ho, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

898
53:06.511 --> 53:10.353
Flowers bloom but make no sound! Birds cry but shed no tears!

899
53:10.353 --> 53:15.303
Love burns but leaves no smoke! Marines die but leave no words!

900
53:15.893 --> 53:18.737
I will do my best!

901
53:18.737 --> 53:21.115
Pilseung!

902
53:21.115 --> 53:25.247
1136th Class! Sergeant Kang Mu Jeok!

903
53:25.247 --> 53:29.248
[Sergeant Kang Mu Jeok, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

904
53:29.248 --> 53:34.030
Like my name, I'll kill the enemy with invincible Marine spirit

905
53:34.030 --> 53:36.422
and bathe in their blood!

906
53:36.422 --> 53:38.048
Pilseung!

907
53:38.048 --> 53:41.751
1147th Class! Corporal Park Cheol Yong!

908
53:41.751 --> 53:45.593
[Corporal Park Cheol Yong, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

909
53:45.593 --> 53:51.125
I'll twist the necks of every enemy I see and use them as wine cups for my comrades!

910
53:51.125 --> 53:53.605
Pilseung!

911
53:53.605 --> 53:57.856
1151st Class! Corporal Seong Gi Jung!

912
53:57.856 --> 54:00.824
[Corporal Seong Gi Jung, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

913
54:00.824 --> 54:04.117
1158th Class! Private First Class Jeong Woo Cheol!

914
54:04.117 --> 54:06.879
[Private First Class Jeong Woo Cheol, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

915
54:06.879 --> 54:10.227
1163rd Class! Private Choi Uk!

916
54:10.227 --> 54:14.533
[Private Choi Uk, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

917
54:14.533 --> 54:16.576
I'll be the first to charge

918
54:16.576 --> 54:21.503
and offer my flesh and bones as fertilizer for the Marine Corps!

919
54:24.306 --> 54:25.824
Stop it!

920
54:27.633 --> 54:29.579
Chungseong!

921
54:29.579 --> 54:32.198
As for me, I am the Lieutenant

922
54:32.198 --> 54:34.273
serving as the Opposing Force Platoon Leader for this exercise,

923
54:34.273 --> 54:36.936
- Oh... - Everyone, attention!

924
54:37.546 --> 54:39.533
Pilseung!

925
54:39.533 --> 54:41.973
Pilseung!

926
54:42.654 --> 54:47.514
First Lieutenant Oh Kang Cheol, Platoon Leader of the Marine Landing Raider Battalion.

927
54:47.514 --> 54:50.913
[First Lieutenant Oh Kang Cheol, Marine Landing Raider Battalion]

928
54:50.913 --> 54:54.092
Army personnel, I look forward to working with you.

929
54:55.393 --> 54:59.264
- Wait, aren't you the Marine from the foxhole? - We meet again.

930
54:59.264 --> 55:02.803
You were an officer? Then why didn't you identify yourself earlier?

931
55:02.803 --> 55:06.277
Marines do not identify themselves to other branches.

932
55:07.253 --> 55:10.473
Hey, even so, you could clearly see the company commander's rank insignia...

933
55:10.473 --> 55:12.709
- The salute was... - Marines!

934
55:12.709 --> 55:17.733
For our Army comrades, get ready to clap!

935
55:17.733 --> 55:21.401
Clap so hard it's heard from heaven to hell! Start clapping!

936
55:21.401 --> 55:23.267
One, two!

937
55:23.267 --> 55:26.972
Sing a military song while clapping! The song is...

938
55:26.972 --> 55:28.813
"The Man in the Octagonal Hat!"

939
55:28.813 --> 55:30.702
- "The Man in the Octagonal Hat!" - "The Man in the Octagonal Hat!"

940
55:30.702 --> 55:32.713
Start singing!

941
55:32.713 --> 55:34.689
One, two, three, four.

942
55:34.689 --> 55:37.960
♪ Octagonal hat, camouflage pattern ♪

943
55:37.960 --> 55:41.178
Why the hell are they suddenly singing?

944
55:42.130 --> 55:45.473
♪ Riding the dark blue waves ♪

945
55:45.473 --> 55:47.799
- What are you doing? - ♪ We go forth ♪

946
55:47.799 --> 55:50.058
My father was in the Marine Corps.

947
55:50.058 --> 55:53.893
- ♪ This land, my motherland ♪ - Are you acting tough over a red name tag?

948
55:53.893 --> 55:57.152
♪ Protecting it together ♪

949
55:57.152 --> 56:00.575
♪ Through the sea of fire ♪

950
56:00.575 --> 56:04.656
♪ We are Marines ♪

951
56:04.656 --> 56:08.338
♪ Octagonal hat, octagonal hat ♪

952
56:08.338 --> 56:11.630
♪ The Man in the Octagonal Hat ♪

953
56:12.327 --> 56:20.172
♪ We are the cool men in octagonal hats ♪

954
56:23.233 --> 56:24.822
- Halt! - Halt.

955
56:24.822 --> 56:26.725
At ease!

956
56:28.353 --> 56:30.682
Now, that's enough for greetings.

957
56:30.682 --> 56:32.913
Army personnel... sit down.

958
56:32.913 --> 56:34.113
At ease, at ease.

959
56:34.113 --> 56:36.051
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

960
56:38.395 --> 56:40.638
- Man, I'm exhausted. - Gosh.

961
56:41.513 --> 56:43.457
Gosh, my back!

962
56:45.053 --> 56:47.425
- Here are the rations for the opposing force. - Oh, cup noodles!

963
56:47.425 --> 56:49.167
- Oh, ramen! - Guys,

964
56:49.167 --> 56:51.950
go to the water station for hot water...

965
56:53.373 --> 56:55.990
Hey! Hurry up! The hot water will run out!

966
56:55.990 --> 56:58.644
Hey! Run, run!

967
57:09.544 --> 57:13.459
- We're too late... - Damn... I feel like I'm going to puke...

968
57:17.942 --> 57:19.686
That's a lot...

969
57:19.686 --> 57:21.650
Isn't he using it all?

970
57:35.973 --> 57:39.590
- What is he smirking at? - That private is so annoying.

971
57:41.093 --> 57:44.133
It's lukewarm. Damn, the hot water's gone.

972
57:44.133 --> 57:45.973
Won't the Marines share some with us?

973
57:45.973 --> 57:49.853
- Hey, have some pride! Forget it! - Are you really not going to eat?

974
57:49.853 --> 57:52.840
- Then can I have yours? - You little punk...

975
57:59.017 --> 58:02.426
Pilseung! Private Choi Uk!

976
58:02.426 --> 58:07.437
I would like to know if I may be permitted to ask Marine Park Cheol Yong if I may report

977
58:07.437 --> 58:12.153
that I have completed securing hot water faster than the other forces as of this time!

978
58:12.153 --> 58:15.328
What? Fuck, hot water?

979
58:16.747 --> 58:19.313
You're a disgrace to the Marines!

980
58:19.313 --> 58:21.753
- Assey! - Private! Choi! Uk!

981
58:21.753 --> 58:23.913
We are the Marine Corps Amphibious Raid Battalion!

982
58:23.913 --> 58:27.215
Hot water doesn't suit a Marine!

983
58:28.630 --> 58:33.352
A true Marine, in a pitch-black field, whether it's rebar or rocks,

984
58:33.352 --> 58:37.553
must have the grit to chew and swallow anything with pure "gonzo!"

985
58:37.553 --> 58:42.769
Therefore, we shall hand over this luxurious hot water to the Army!

986
58:42.769 --> 58:43.843
Execute!

987
58:43.843 --> 58:46.068
- Yes! - Look at that spirit.

988
58:46.068 --> 58:47.468
Yes!

989
58:49.979 --> 58:52.428
Assey! You eat it.

990
58:52.428 --> 58:54.225
Thank you.

991
58:58.593 --> 59:01.039
- Thank you. - Thank you.

992
59:18.509 --> 59:20.811
- This is so delicious. - It's great.

993
59:20.811 --> 59:23.453
Who said there were no chopsticks?

994
59:23.453 --> 59:27.417
- I found them. - Why did you say there weren't any?

995
59:28.116 --> 59:29.711
It's hot, it's hot.

996
59:33.913 --> 59:38.053
- Bit Na Ri, take a hint, you punk. - I'm sorry.

997
59:38.053 --> 59:42.933
- Hey, our Assey should have one too! - Thank you, sir!

998
59:56.792 --> 01:00:00.042
- Assey! - Private Choi Uk!

999
01:00:01.219 --> 01:00:03.270
What are you looking at right now?

1000
01:00:03.270 --> 01:00:08.353
Are the eyes of a sacred Marine wavering over something like ramen?

1001
01:00:08.353 --> 01:00:10.973
Private Choi Uk! I will do better!

1002
01:00:10.973 --> 01:00:12.555
Listen up, Assey!

1003
01:00:12.555 --> 01:00:15.173
A Marine does not feel hunger!

1004
01:00:15.173 --> 01:00:18.994
Even your own saliva, you must chew and swallow with pure grit!

1005
01:00:18.994 --> 01:00:21.379
- Understood? - Yes, sir!

1006
01:00:22.494 --> 01:00:24.750
Corporal Park Cheol Yong?

1007
01:00:24.750 --> 01:00:28.373
Why don't you let the newbie eat in peace?

1008
01:00:28.373 --> 01:00:30.851
Marines take care of their own.

1009
01:00:30.851 --> 01:00:33.673
The Army doesn't need to worry.

1010
01:00:33.673 --> 01:00:37.493
Fine, do that then... Why so angry, geez...

1011
01:00:37.493 --> 01:00:39.331
I've lost my appetite.

1012
01:00:41.308 --> 01:00:45.419
- Ramen tastes best during training. - You're right.

1013
01:00:47.189 --> 01:00:48.978
It's delicious.

1014
01:00:56.163 --> 01:01:00.243
Did you see Moon Bit Na Ri offering ramen to that Marine?

1015
01:01:00.243 --> 01:01:02.583
Was he trying to mess with him on purpose?

1016
01:01:02.583 --> 01:01:07.183
You know how clueless he is. He was 100% sincere, I bet.

1017
01:01:07.183 --> 01:01:09.582
He's as clueless as you, right?

1018
01:01:09.582 --> 01:01:11.563
Hey, why are you like this?

1019
01:01:11.563 --> 01:01:14.703
"Why are you like this?" You're getting lazy, you punk.

1020
01:01:14.703 --> 01:01:17.261
I am not getting lazy.

1021
01:01:17.261 --> 01:01:19.061
Pilseung!

1022
01:01:20.764 --> 01:01:24.803
Pilseung! To Sergeant Kim Sang Hun! I am currently at the latrine,

1023
01:01:24.803 --> 01:01:28.602
and I am reporting to ask if I may inquire about the possibility of

1024
01:01:28.602 --> 01:01:32.592
requesting permission to commence urination!

1025
01:01:35.223 --> 01:01:37.063
You crazy bastard! That's a spot-on impression!

1026
01:01:37.063 --> 01:01:39.853
I actually wanted to join the Marines...
